    <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">NUTRITION STUDENT CLUB ACTIVITIES</div>
    <p>This year Club President {{ president_name }} and her leadership team were very productive. There were opportunities for students to become involved in community, industry and school-oriented projects and to meet with career professionals, faculty, and other students.</p>
    <p>In addition, scholarships to local conferences and state professional conventions were offered. Other events sponsored by the Club included: presentations by speakers on all facets of nutrition and food science, planning the Department's Convocation ceremony, and holding regular Club meetings.</p>
    <p>The Club also managed the Department's "Smart Cart" that offers all SJSU students the opportunity to purchase healthy snacks and beverages such as bottled water, cheese sticks, fresh organic fruit, granola bars, yogurt and vegan snack bars.</p>

    <div class="section-title" style="margin-top: 30px;">PACKAGING PROGRAM STUDENT HIGHLIGHTS</div>
    <p>The Packaging Program led by Dr. {{ faculty_name_pkg }} had a terrific year. Twenty-five Packaging students visited Chicago for the PMI Pack Expo, a national packaging show. The students had a booth representing SJSU. At the show, the Packaging students competed in the "AMAZING PACKAGING RACE" where they built a packaging product to specifications provided by participating machine operators.</p>
    <p>In addition, twenty-five Packaging students visited Intuitive Surgical to view the manufacturing of the Da Vinci Robotic Surgery System. Also, Packaging students entered the American Forest Products (AFP) Paperboard Packaging Competition and placed well in a field of {{ number_of_placements }} applicants. The AFP awarded $3,000 in student scholarships. Other Packaging students included $1,500 from the Healthcare Compliance Council (HCC) and $3,500 from the Schuenemann Scholarship Fund.</p>
